  "summary": "Variant-effect and ligand-scoring predictors now train on MD, force-field energy and residue-atom geometry rather than sequence statistics alone, feeding closed-loop design.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is grafting physical supervision onto sequence foundation models. DynamicsPLM adds residue-level and pairwise molecular-dynamics heads to a 35M-parameter PLM for zero-shot mutation effects; MutAtlas assembles a PDB-wide atlas of exhaustive single-site mutations scored jointly by energy, language-model and inverse-folding terms; ProTEUS pretrains a mutation-resolved world model on deep mutational scanning coupled to a fast physics-constrained all-atom predictor for closed-loop evolution. The same fusion appears on the ligand side: BioLM-Score combines frozen protein and molecular LM embeddings with residue-atom geometric likelihoods, RSMBind pairs RNA language-model embeddings with 3D descriptors for nucleotide-level small-molecule sites, and a systematic benchmark probes zero-shot PLM/SMILES binding-site prediction. What is new is the shift from embeddings-as-features to explicit energetic and dynamical labels, plus actionable layers on top: PAMP projects a differentiable turnover objective onto discrete substitutions, and Pyrite casts cofolding pose ranking as an agentic task.",
